{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113000","id":3031956855,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc60t_13","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113000","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113000.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113000.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113000","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113000/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113000/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113000/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/17703ab0fb6f0a5d096403e7fbc54145259acc3c","number":113000,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix corruption of D3D12 CPU descriptor heap free blocks","user":{"login":"brycehutchings","id":5100250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDAyNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5100250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings","html_url":"https://github.com/brycehutchings","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While running my own build of Godot 4.5.1 I was seeing heap corruption in D3D12 code. To investigate I made a dev build and found I was hitting a dev assert in the D3D12 CPU descriptor heap management logic:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1342\" height=\"694\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c042ba2-15ca-4075-acbe-c967e350e522\" />\r\n\r\nI believe the problem due to the order of deletion and update, specifically:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nfree_blocks_by_offset.erase(next->value.global_offset);\r\n```\r\n\r\n`next->value.global_offset` always matches the key of the pair in this RBMap, so this is erasing \"next\" itself. So the `next` iterator now points to deleted memory, but then `next` is updated and put back into free_blocks_by_offset. Since `next` points to deleted memory, this is undefined behavior. In my debug builds, you can see in the screenshot that some kind of sentinel values get set to make this \"use-after-free\" issue more obvious.\r\n\r\nTo fix this I create a block separate from the one that `next` points to so I can mutate it before deleting the old block and inserting in the new merged block. I don't know if this fixes the original heap corruption but it does fix the DEV_ASSERT (on line 497 in my screenshot) and corrupted block data.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":205417413,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDU0MTc0MTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:windows","name":"platform:windows","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}